    "The route requires 180 EC. Its selected branches nominally sum to 180 but four repeated 5 EC codes reduce the unique-code total to 160. Two Philosophy of Science versions show the same core content; the 5 EC is counted once. The catalogue narrative places it in year two.",
    "The first-year seminar requires concurrent History of the Ancient Near East. Papyrological Sources requires Ancient History and the binding study advice threshold. The selected Constantine seminar requires passed Ancient History and the first-year ONOS seminar. The Roman North Africa module lists History-specific prerequisites without an explicit ONOS entry path. The thesis and thesis seminar require completion of years one and two, and participation in the seminar is mandatory.",
